["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Old hands come home every time because they expect trouble before it starts. Know how people really get lost, and you stop being one of them.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The 10 chapters of the Safety and Navigation Masterclass: 1 why people get lost and hurt, 2 the never get lost system, 3 reading a topo map, 4 the compass, 5 map plus land, 6 phone, GPS and the Hunt Map, 7 when you think you are lost, 8 surviving the night, 9 avoiding risky situations, 10 drills and the cheat sheet.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Safety and Navigation Masterclass</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"42.0\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"68.6\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1 Why people get lost</text><rect x=\"205.0\" y=\"42.0\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"68.6\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2 Never get lost system</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"93.2\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"119.80000000000001\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3 Reading a topo map</text><rect x=\"205.0\" y=\"93.2\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"119.80000000000001\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4 The compass</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"144.4\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"171.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5 Map plus land</text><rect x=\"205.0\" y=\"144.4\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"171.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6 Phone, GPS, Hunt Map</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"195.60000000000002\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"222.20000000000002\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">7 When you are lost</text><rect x=\"205.0\" y=\"195.60000000000002\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"222.20000000000002\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">8 Surviving the night</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"246.8\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"273.40000000000003\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">9 Avoiding risk</text><rect x=\"205.0\" y=\"246.8\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"43.2\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"273.40000000000003\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">10 Drills, cheat sheet</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>10 chapters on staying found, finding your way back, and getting through a bad night.</li><li>This chapter: the real causes, the traps in your head, and the trip plan.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what the 10 chapters cover</summary><ol><li>Why people get lost and hurt (this one): search and rescue numbers, how hunters get lost, the risk mindset, the trip plan and when to call.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-02\">The never get lost system</a>: handrails, backstops, baselines, look back, checks every 15 to 30 minutes, stop when unsure.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-03\">Reading a topo map</a>: scale, contours, landforms, symbols, UTM (Universal Transverse Mercator) grid, declination.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-04\">The compass</a>: bearings, leapfrogging, back bearings, cross bearings, aiming off, errors.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-05\">Map plus land together</a>: orienting, terrain association, finding where you are, sun and shadows.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-06\">Phone, GPS and the Hunt Map</a>: offline maps, truck pin, Back to start, battery, satellite help.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-07\">When you think you're lost</a>: STOP, stay or move, calling, signals, helping searchers.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-08\">Surviving the night</a>: shelter, fire, warmth, water, hypothermia, the kit.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-09\">Avoiding risky situations</a>: dark and weather, cliffs, water and ice, boats, ATV (all terrain vehicle), wildlife, firearms, fatigue.</li><li><a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-10\">Drills and cheat sheet</a>: four practice plans, the one page cheat sheet, links.</li></ol><ul><li>Flashcards: the \"Safety and Navigation Masterclass\" deck.</li><li>Every fact has a certainty %. 95 to 100: read in an official source. 80 to 94: official, some reading. 60 to 79: good secondary source. Under 60%: labelled Tip or <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>\"Old hand's rule\" lines are tradition and opinion, not fact.</li><li>The foundation lessons stay the quick versions: <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety\">Bush safety</a>, <a href=\"#/s/lost-survival-kit\">Lost and the survival kit</a>, <a href=\"#/s/compass-mastery\">Compass mastery</a>, <a href=\"#/s/gps-phone-battery\">GPS, phone and battery</a>. This Masterclass links to them and goes deeper.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of BC ground search and rescue tasks in 2022 by activity: hiking 41 percent, other outdoor recreation 26 percent, biking 11, driving 8, skiing 7, sledding 7. 1,510 tasks in all. Source: BC Search and Rescue Association 2022 review, my reading of its chart, 80 percent.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">BC ground SAR tasks, 2022</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"67.83333333333333\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Hiking</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"50.78\" width=\"190.0\" height=\"24.106666666666666\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"336.0\" y=\"67.83333333333333\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">41%</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"105.49999999999999\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Other outdoor</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"88.44666666666666\" width=\"120.48780487804878\" height=\"24.106666666666666\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"266.4878048780488\" y=\"105.49999999999999\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">26%</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"143.16666666666666\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Biking</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"126.11333333333333\" width=\"50.97560975609756\" height=\"24.106666666666666\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"196.97560975609755\" y=\"143.16666666666666\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">11%</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"180.83333333333334\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Driving</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"163.78\" width=\"37.073170731707314\" height=\"24.106666666666666\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"183.0731707317073\" y=\"180.83333333333334\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">8%</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"218.5\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Skiing</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"201.44666666666666\" width=\"32.4390243902439\" height=\"24.106666666666666\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"178.4390243902439\" y=\"218.5\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">7%</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"256.16666666666663\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Sledding</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"239.11333333333332\" width=\"32.4390243902439\" height=\"24.106666666666666\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"178.4390243902439\" y=\"256.16666666666663\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">7%</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1,510 tasks. BCSARA 2022 review (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>BC ground search and rescue had 1,510 tasks in 2022 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Hiking was the biggest slice, about 41% <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the 2022 numbers in full</summary><ul><li>BCSARA (BC Search and Rescue Association) 2022 Year in Review: 1,510 GSAR (ground search and rescue) tasks, 2,087 team deployments, 67 callouts longer than 24 hours (95%, read directly).</li><li>1,019 lives saved in 2022; more than 10,000 in the past 10 years <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>\"12% involved subjects who would have died without urgent GSAR intervention and 43% involved subjects who would have ultimately not survived\" without it <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Activity chart: hiking 41%, other recreational activities 26%, biking 11%, driving 8%, skiing 7%, sledding 7% (80%, my reading of the chart labels).</li><li>Hunting has no slice of its own in that chart <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. It sits inside \"other\" (Tip, my reading).</li><li>Calls have grown: just under 1,000 in 2003, a record 2,100 in 2021, about 1,500 in 2022 (75%, Global News, 2023).</li><li>BC rescue volunteers do not charge you: \"you don't pay to be rescued\" (95%, sponsor quote in the BCSARA report). North Shore Rescue says the same: \"there is no cost for rescue\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>GSAR teams are called out by agencies such as police, BC Ambulance and fire services, not by you directly. You call 911 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"BC Search and Rescue Association list of the top 10 worst things you can do: 1 wrong footwear, 2 no trip plan, 3 recreating above your skills, 4 thinking easy access means an easy hike, 5 going with only a cell phone and maybe some water, 6 not thinking what if, 7 not knowing your location, 8 relying on search and rescue for preventable incidents, 9 being over confident, 10 being under prepared. Items 2, 5, 6 and 7 are highlighted as the ones this chapter fixes.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">SAR&#x27;s 10 worst things you can do</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"44.0\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"59.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"59.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wrong footwear</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"67.5\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f6d7c3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"82.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"82.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">No trip plan</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"91.0\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"106.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"106.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Above your skills</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"114.5\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"129.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"129.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Easy access, easy hike?</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"138.0\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f6d7c3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"153.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"153.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Only a phone and some water</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"161.5\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f6d7c3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"176.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"176.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">No &quot;what if&quot;</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"185.0\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f6d7c3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">7</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Not knowing your location</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"208.5\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"223.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">8</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"223.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Preventable callouts</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"232.0\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"247.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">9</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"247.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Over confident</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"255.5\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"270.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">10</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"270.5\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Under prepared</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"293\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BCSARA 2022 review. Orange: this chapter (95%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>BCSARA's top 10 worst things you can do <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Four of them are pure navigation and planning: no trip plan, only a phone, no \"what if\", not knowing your location.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the list word for word</summary><p>BC Search and Rescue Association, 2022 Year in Review, \"Top 10 worst things you can do\" (95%, read directly):</p><ol><li>Wearing inappropriate footwear (causing slips, trips, falls and broken bones).</li><li>Not leaving a trip plan with a trusted emergency contact.</li><li>Assessing your skills wrongly and recreating above your abilities.</li><li>Thinking easy access to a trail equals an easy hike.</li><li>Going into the mountains with ONLY a cell phone and \"maybe\" some water.</li><li>Not thinking \"what if\" (what if I break my ankle, get lost or have to spend the night).</li><li>Not knowing your location (such as latitude and longitude).</li><li>Relying on search and rescue volunteers for incidents that could be preventable.</li><li>Being over confident, not aware of risks.</li><li>Being under prepared and misinformed.</li></ol><ul><li>News coverage of BCSARA data: the top three hiking emergencies were getting lost or having no navigation device, poor footwear, and not knowing how hard the trail is; together 271 calls in 2022 (70%, CTV and North Shore News, search preview).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How hunters get lost: 1 Eyes on the deer or the blood; 2 Off the trail, into thick brush; 3 No look back, no map check; 4 Light fades, ground looks new; 5 Drifts downhill, off trail. Koester lost person data, via Popular Science (65%)\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">How hunters get lost</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"42\" width=\"320\" height=\"38.8\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"61.4\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"64\" y=\"66.4\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"66.4\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eyes on the deer or the blood</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"80.8\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"83.8\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"200.0,90.8 203.5,83.8 196.5,83.8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"90.8\" width=\"320\" height=\"38.8\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"110.19999999999999\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"64\" y=\"115.19999999999999\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"115.19999999999999\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Off the trail, into thick brush</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"129.6\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"132.6\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"200.0,139.6 203.5,132.6 196.5,132.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"139.6\" width=\"320\" height=\"38.8\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"159.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"64\" y=\"164.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"164.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">No look back, no map check</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"178.39999999999998\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"181.39999999999998\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"200.0,188.4 203.5,181.4 196.5,181.4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"188.39999999999998\" width=\"320\" height=\"38.8\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"207.79999999999998\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"64\" y=\"212.79999999999998\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"212.79999999999998\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Light fades, ground looks new</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"227.2\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"230.2\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"200.0,237.2 203.5,230.2 196.5,230.2\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"237.2\" width=\"320\" height=\"38.8\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6d7c3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"256.59999999999997\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"64\" y=\"261.59999999999997\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"86\" y=\"261.59999999999997\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Drifts downhill, off trail</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Koester lost person data, via Popular Science (65%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Hunters usually get lost following an animal or a blood trail through thick brush <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Eyes on the game, not on the way back.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what the lost person research says</summary><ul><li>Robert Koester built the ISRID (International Search and Rescue Incident Database), now about 300,000 incidents (65%, Popular Science and Undark, 2024).</li><li>Hunters \"usually get lost because they followed an animal intently through dense brush\" (65%, same article quoting Koester's book Lost Person Behavior).</li><li>Koester: the most common reason is \"spatial disorientation, often related to intense concentration following game or a blood trail\" (60%, search preview of the same reporting).</li><li>Lost hunters tend to head downhill and off trail <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. More in <a href=\"#/s/mc-nav-07\">Chapter 7</a>.</li><li>Under cloud in a forest, people walk in circles without knowing it (75%, Max Planck Institute, 2009, see <a href=\"#/s/lost-survival-kit\">Lost</a>).</li><li>Hunter specific risks (Tip): starting in the dark, finishing in the dark, leaving the trail on purpose, chasing a wounded animal, hunting alone, carrying a heavy pack late in the day.</li><li>Every blood trail needs a plan for the way out: flag the last blood, drop a waypoint, check the time (<a href=\"#/s/mc-skills-08\">After the shot</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A chain of five links: late start, wrong turn, dark comes, wet and cold, a fall or a bad call. Break any link and the chain fails; a turnaround time breaks the first three. Tip, hunter wisdom.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Small problems stack up</text><rect x=\"24\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Late start</text><rect x=\"144\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wrong turn</text><rect x=\"264\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dark comes</text><rect x=\"74\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wet and cold</text><rect x=\"214\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#f6d7c3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Fall, bad call</text><line x1=\"136\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"136.0\" y2=\"72.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"144.0,72.0 136.0,68.0 136.0,76.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"256\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"256.0\" y2=\"72.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"264.0,72.0 256.0,68.0 256.0,76.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"98\" x2=\"168.5859434521113\" y2=\"139.30156062933645\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"160.0,142.0 169.9,143.6 167.2,135.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"186\" y1=\"168\" x2=\"206.0\" y2=\"168.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"214.0,168.0 206.0,164.0 206.0,172.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Break any link and the chain fails.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Turnaround time breaks the first three.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip: hunter wisdom</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most bad nights start as small slips that pile up (Tip).</li><li>Break one link early and the chain fails.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how a normal hunt turns bad</summary><ul><li>Example chain (Tip): a late start, so you hurry; a wrong turn while chasing a deer; dark comes; you are sweaty and the wind picks up; you slip on a wet log in the dark.</li><li>Each link is small. Together they make a search and rescue call (Tip).</li><li>BCSARA's own list matches: no \"what if\" thinking, poor footwear, over confidence <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>The cheapest link to break is time: a turnaround time set at home (Tip, see <a href=\"#/s/route-planning\">Planning a route</a>).</li><li>The second cheapest: a trip plan, so the night is short even if it goes wrong (75%, AdventureSmart).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The six FACETS heuristic traps found in avalanche accidents, with a hunter example each: Familiarity, I know this hill; Acceptance, do not look weak; Consistency, came this far; Expert halo, he knows best; Scarcity, last day; Social facilitation, others went. Source McCammon via avalanche.org, 80 percent. Hunter examples are Tip.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Six traps in your head</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"42.0\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"72.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"75.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">F Familiarity</text><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"94.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;I know this hill&quot;</text><rect x=\"205.0\" y=\"42.0\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"72.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"75.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A Acceptance</text><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"94.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;Don&#x27;t look weak&quot;</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"122.0\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"72.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"155.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">C Consistency</text><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"174.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;Came this far&quot;</text><rect x=\"205.0\" y=\"122.0\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"72.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"155.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">E Expert halo</text><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"174.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;He knows best&quot;</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"202.0\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"72.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"235.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">T Scarcity</text><text x=\"107.5\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;Last day!&quot;</text><rect x=\"205.0\" y=\"202.0\" width=\"175.0\" height=\"72.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"235.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">S Social</text><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;Others went&quot;</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">FACETS, McCammon via avalanche.org (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Avalanche research found six thinking traps in accidents: FACETS <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>They fit hunting too. Name the trap, then decide (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: FACETS and the hunter version</summary><ul><li>Ian McCammon studied recreational avalanche accidents and named six \"heuristic traps\" (80%, avalanche.org encyclopedia):<ul><li><strong>Familiarity:</strong> \"Parties traveling in familiar terrain tend to make riskier decisions.\"</li><li><strong>Acceptance:</strong> people take more risk to be accepted by their group.</li><li><strong>Consistency:</strong> parties \"highly committed to a goal\", even in worsening weather.</li><li><strong>Expert halo:</strong> a de facto leader, older or more experienced, whom others follow.</li><li><strong>Tracks or scarcity:</strong> more risk when \"racing a closing window of opportunity\".</li><li><strong>Social facilitation:</strong> groups get bolder when other parties are around.</li></ul></li><li>The hunter versions below are my application, not from the research (Tip):<ul><li>Familiarity: \"I hunted this draw last year, no need for the map.\"</li><li>Acceptance: \"I won't tell my brother I'm unsure.\"</li><li>Consistency: \"One more ridge, we came this far.\" Or \"keep following the blood.\"</li><li>Expert halo: \"He's been here before, I'll just follow.\"</li><li>Scarcity: \"Last day of the season, last hour of light.\"</li><li>Social: \"Other trucks are parked up here, so the road must be fine.\"</li></ul></li><li>McCammon's work shows links, not causes, because it is based on accident data (75%, search preview).</li><li>Avalanche risk itself: <a href=\"#/s/avalanche-hunters\">Avalanche awareness</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A trip plan card with seven lines: who is going; the vehicle, plate and colour; where it is parked with road name and coordinates; route with plan A and plan B; back by clock time; call 911 if no word by a set time; gear such as satellite SOS and orange clothing. Leave it with someone who is not on the trip, 75 percent, AdventureSmart.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The trip plan card</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"40\" width=\"280\" height=\"236\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3efe0\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"74\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Who</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">you, your brother</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"75\" x2=\"326\" y2=\"75\" stroke=\"#d8cfb4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"74\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Vehicle</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">truck, plate, colour</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"105\" x2=\"326\" y2=\"105\" stroke=\"#d8cfb4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"74\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Parked</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">road name, coordinates</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"326\" y2=\"135\" stroke=\"#d8cfb4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"74\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Route</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">plan A and plan B</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"165\" x2=\"326\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#d8cfb4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"74\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Back by</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">clock time</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"326\" y2=\"195\" stroke=\"#d8cfb4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"74\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Call 911 if</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">no word by ...</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"225\" x2=\"326\" y2=\"225\" stroke=\"#d8cfb4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"74\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Gear</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">satellite SOS, orange</text><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"255\" x2=\"326\" y2=\"255\" stroke=\"#d8cfb4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"293\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Leave it with someone not on the trip (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Leave a trip plan with someone not on the trip, every time <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Add coordinates for the truck and a \"call 911 if\" time (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the trip plan in full</summary><ul><li>AdventureSmart's Three Ts: trip planning, training, taking the essentials (75%, via <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety\">Bush safety</a>).</li><li>BCSARA's number 2 worst thing: no trip plan with a trusted emergency contact <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>North Shore Rescue: \"Leave a Trip Plan with a Friend, so someone will notice if you're overdue\" (75%, read directly).</li><li>What to write (75% for the core items, Tip for the extras):<ul><li>Who: names, phone numbers, any medical issues.</li><li>Vehicle: make, colour, plate. Trailer, ATV or boat if you bring them.</li><li>Where parked: road name and kilometre sign if there is one, plus coordinates from the Hunt Map (tap the elevation readout for Map centre and copy them, 99%, app).</li><li>Route: plan A and plan B for the other wind.</li><li>Back by: a clock time. Call 911 if: a later clock time.</li><li>Gear: satellite SOS on the phone or a messenger, colours of your jacket and pack.</li></ul></li><li>AdventureSmart has a free trip plan tool (75%, see <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety\">Bush safety</a>).</li><li>Hunt Mentor's <a href=\"#/plan\">Plan a hunt</a> screen helps you build the day.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"mc-nav-tripplan-check\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"mc-nav-tripplan-check:0\"><span>Who, phone numbers, medical notes</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"mc-nav-tripplan-check:1\"><span>Vehicle, colour, plate</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"mc-nav-tripplan-check:2\"><span>Where parked, with coordinates</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"mc-nav-tripplan-check:3\"><span>Route: plan A and plan B</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"mc-nav-tripplan-check:4\"><span>Back by time</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"mc-nav-tripplan-check:5\"><span>Call 911 if no word by time</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"mc-nav-tripplan-check:6\"><span>Jacket and pack colours</span></label></div>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timeline of an example mid October evening near Heffley Creek: turn around at 16:15, at the truck by 17:40, text home at 18:00, and home calls 911 at 21:00 if there is no word. Sunset about 18:08, my calculation, 85 percent. The times are an example, a Tip, not a rule.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Example evening: who does what</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"150\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">16:15</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Turn around</text><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"150\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">17:40</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">At truck</text><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"150\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">18:00</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Text home</text><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"150\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">21:00</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Home calls 911</text><circle cx=\"355\" cy=\"70\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#f4b400\"/><line x1=\"371.0\" y1=\"70.0\" x2=\"377.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#f4b400\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"366.31370849898474\" y1=\"81.31370849898477\" x2=\"370.55634918610406\" y2=\"85.55634918610404\" stroke=\"#f4b400\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"355.0\" y1=\"86.0\" x2=\"355.0\" y2=\"92.0\" stroke=\"#f4b400\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"343.68629150101526\" y1=\"81.31370849898477\" x2=\"339.44365081389594\" y2=\"85.55634918610404\" stroke=\"#f4b400\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"339.0\" y1=\"70.0\" x2=\"333.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#f4b400\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"343.68629150101526\" y1=\"58.68629150101524\" x2=\"339.44365081389594\" y2=\"54.44365081389596\" stroke=\"#f4b400\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"355.0\" y1=\"54.0\" x2=\"355.0\" y2=\"48.0\" stroke=\"#f4b400\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"366.31370849898474\" y1=\"58.68629150101523\" x2=\"370.55634918610406\" y2=\"54.44365081389595\" stroke=\"#f4b400\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"end\">Sunset 18:08</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mid October, Heffley Creek. Times are an</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">example, not a rule (Tip).</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sunset: my calculation (85%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Pick the \"call 911 if\" time before you leave (Tip).</li><li>You call too, early, as soon as you know you are lost or hurt <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the calling rules</summary><ul><li>North Shore Rescue: \"dial 9-1-1 as soon as you know you're lost or injured\"; \"early callouts help NSR find you before conditions worsen\" (75%, read directly).</li><li>For a search and rescue emergency, dial 911 and ask for police (75%, North Shore Rescue).</li><li>A BCSARA story: a lost hiker hesitated, thinking 911 was only for people in immediate danger. The advice was \"call for help and call early\" (95%, BCSARA 2022 review).</li><li>Example evening for mid October at Heffley Creek (Tip): turn around 16:15, at the truck 17:40, text home 18:00, home calls 911 at 21:00 with no word.</li><li>Mid October sunset there is about 18:08 (85%, my calculation). Legal light for big game ends 1 hour after sunset (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Rule Book: legal methods</a>).</li><li>The person at home needs the plan, your plate, and the instruction \"call 911, ask for police, read them this\" (Tip).</li><li>Rules for when to stop hunting: Rule Book only. This screen adds no rules.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Beginner</th><th>Old hand (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>\"Just up the road\", no plan</td><td>Trip plan every time</td></tr><tr><td>Phone only</td><td>Phone, paper map, compass</td></tr><tr><td>Follows the blood, eyes down</td><td>Flags, pins, looks back</td></tr><tr><td>Pushes for one more ridge</td><td>Turns around on time</td></tr><tr><td>Calls when it is dark</td><td>Calls when unsure</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Every line is hunter and search and rescue wisdom, labelled Tip.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: where these come from</summary><ul><li>Trip plan every time: BCSARA top 10 and AdventureSmart (75 to 95%).</li><li>Phone plus paper and compass: BCSARA \"only a cell phone\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>; <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety\">Bush safety</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Flag and pin a blood trail: <a href=\"#/s/mc-skills-08\">After the shot</a> (Tip).</li><li>Turnaround time: North Shore Rescue \"set a clear turnaround time\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Call early: North Shore Rescue <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A chain of five links: late start, wrong turn, dark comes, wet and cold, a fall or a bad call. Break any link and the chain fails; a turnaround time breaks the first three. Tip, hunter wisdom.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Small problems stack up</text><rect x=\"24\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Late start</text><rect x=\"144\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wrong turn</text><rect x=\"264\" y=\"48\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dark comes</text><rect x=\"74\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wet and cold</text><rect x=\"214\" y=\"144\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#f6d7c3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Fall, bad call</text><line x1=\"136\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"136.0\" y2=\"72.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"144.0,72.0 136.0,68.0 136.0,76.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"256\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"256.0\" y2=\"72.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"264.0,72.0 256.0,68.0 256.0,76.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"98\" x2=\"168.5859434521113\" y2=\"139.30156062933645\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"160.0,142.0 169.9,143.6 167.2,135.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"186\" y1=\"168\" x2=\"206.0\" y2=\"168.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"214.0,168.0 206.0,164.0 206.0,172.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Break any link and the chain fails.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Turnaround time breaks the first three.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip: hunter wisdom</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Eyes on the deer, lost in a year. Eyes on the way, home for the day.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 1,510 tasks in 2022. About 1 in 10 would have died without urgent help (12%, 95%).</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, short form of AdventureSmart's trip plan advice): \"Tell someone, every time.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>FACETS:</strong> Familiarity, Acceptance, Consistency, Expert halo, Tracks or scarcity, Social facilitation <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Call when unsure, not when it's dark.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 2 times: back by, and call 911 if. Both on the plan (Tip).</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, short form of North Shore Rescue's \"call for help early\"): \"Pride costs more than a phone call.\"</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>No trip plan because it is \"only up the road\".</li><li>Following the blood trail without a single look back.</li><li>Waiting until full dark to call.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Tonight: write a trip plan template in your phone notes with every line on the card. Send one for your next scouting trip, even a short one.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://bcsara.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/BCSARA_2022_Year_In_Review_Report.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Search and Rescue Association, 2022 Year in Review (PDF)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: tasks, lives saved, activity chart, top 10 worst things, call early story, no charge (95%; chart reading 80%).</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://globalnews.ca/news/9571096/bc-search-and-rescue-calls-pre-pandemic-levels\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Global News: BC search and rescue calls (2023)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://ctvnews.ca/vancouver/vancouver-island/article/these-10-bc-hikes-required-the-most-rescues-last-year\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CTV News: BC hikes that needed the most rescues</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.popsci.com/environment/the-burgeoning-science-of-search-and-rescue/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Popular Science (Undark): The burgeoning science of search and rescue, 22 January 2024</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: Koester, ISRID, hunters <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://avalanche.org/avalanche-encyclopedia/human/decision-making/human-factors/f-a-c-e-t-s/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">avalanche.org: FACETS</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.northshorerescue.com/education/outdoor-safety/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">North Shore Rescue: Outdoor safety</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul>","<ul><li>AdventureSmart Three Ts and trip plan, via <a href=\"#/s/bush-safety\">Bush safety</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Sunset: my calculation with standard solar equations, as in <a href=\"#/s/route-planning\">Planning a route</a> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Legal light: Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-nav.md</code>.</li></ul>"]